  <underline|Autre exercice de récurrence forte>

  <image|<tuple|<#>|png>|1par|||>

  On a <math|u<rsub|0>=1> et<space|2em><math|u<rsub|n+1>=u<rsub|0>+u<rsub|1>+\<ldots\>u<rsub|n>>

  <math|u<rsub|0>=1>

  <math|u<rsub|1>=1>

  <math|u<rsub|2>=u<rsub|0>+u<rsub|1>=2>

  <math|u<rsub|3>=4>

  <math|u<rsub|4>=8>

  <math|u<rsub|5>=16>

  On cherche à prouver par récurrence (forte) <math|u<rsub|n>=2<rsup|n-1>>

  Initialisat. <math|u<rsub|1>=1> \ <math|1=2<rsup|1-1>> vrai.

  On suppose <math|u<rsub|n>=2<rsup|n-1>> et <math|u<rsub|n-1>=2<rsup|n-2>>
  et <text-dots> <math|u<rsub|1>=2<rsup|1-1>=1> et <math|>

  alors <math|u<rsub|n+1>=u<rsub|0>+u<rsub|1>+\<cdots\>+u<rsub|n>>

  <math|u<rsub|n+1>=1+<around*|(|2<rsup|1-1>+2<rsup|2-1>+\<cdots\>+2<rsup|n-1>|)>>

  <math|u<rsub|n+1>=1+<around*|(|2<rsup|0>+2<rsup|1>+\<cdots\>+2<rsup|n-1>|)>>

  <math|=1+1\<times\><frac|1-2<rsup|n>|1-2>>

  <math|=1+2<rsup|n>-1>

  =<math|2<rsup|n>> = <math|2<rsup|<around*|(|n+1|)>-1>><space|1em>vrai au
  rang <math|n+1>

  Finalement <underline|On a prouvé par récurrence forte sur <math|n> que
  <math|u<rsub|n>=2<rsup|n-1>> pour tout<space|1em><math|n\<in\>\<bbb-N\>>>

